==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystery Yuki & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mystery Catgirl Yuki''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Due to her high damage and decent range, she does well against Floating enemies such as [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and [[The Face]] (or pretty much any Bun Bun or Face variant).

==='''True Form'''===
Mystery Catgirl Yuki gains a few improvements in her True Form, which are [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immunity]], 30 more range and a 1.67 second reduction to her foreswing.

Starting off with range, we find that it is useless for Floating Enemies since no Floatings have a range/[[Omni Strike]] that reaches up to 430-459 range; however, many general enemies have 450 range or under ([[THE SLOTH]] and [[Master A.]], for example), so this greatly improves her performance as a generalist. Next up is Weaken Immunity. The only floating enemies that [[Weaken]] are [[Calamary]] and [[Cli-One]], so this is beneficial in that regard. Finally, the 1.67s reduction to foreswing. This is very good, as it slightly increases Yuki's DPS by allowing her to attack faster, but that's all it does.

In summary, while this True Form doesn't majorly change this unit, it does improve expand upon her generalist and specialist niches. Considering the light Catfruit cost compared to other Ubers, it is recommended to get this.

==='''Talents'''===
Mysterious Catgirl Yuki's Talents are frankly terrible. [[Knockback]] is hardly beneficial in any scenario given Yuki's status as a nuker and long TBA, not to mention the fact that the activation rate only goes up to 50%. [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Toxic]] is irrelevant since she has more than enough range to prevent any Toxic attack from reaching her in the first place, and her effective HP is already so low that she wouldn't be able to tank one regardless. Cost Down only makes her 450¢ cheaper, which is just not worth the 175 NP price tag.

Attack Up is therefore her most worthwhile talent. (However, if you happen to own [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Windy α]], it is generally recommended to invest this NP into her instead.)

==='''Orb'''===
Mystery Catgirl Yuki benefits from the Strengthen Orb or the Floating Massive Damage Orb, although a Toxic Resist Orb also helps her out a lot against [[Gobble]], but it's not recommended compared to the previous options.

